From: Martin Pluskal <martin@pluskal.org>
Subject: do not crash the post-ready worker when the chat is gone

_show_greeting_message() runs inside the non-exclusive worker started by
_start_post_ready_startup(), after an await on the account and identity
refreshes.  When the chat widget is not on the screen by the time that await
returns, query_one("#chat") raises NoMatches out of the worker and Textual
re-raises it at the end of run_test(), failing whichever UI test happened to
be running.  The greeting is cosmetic, so skip it; messages.py already guards
the same lookup this way.

Index: mistral-vibe-2.25.7/vibe/cli/textual_ui/app.py
===================================================================
--- mistral-vibe-2.25.7.orig/vibe/cli/textual_ui/app.py
+++ mistral-vibe-2.25.7/vibe/cli/textual_ui/app.py
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@ from rich import print as rprint
 from textual.app import WINDOWS, App, ComposeResult
 from textual.binding import Binding, BindingType
 from textual.containers import Horizontal, VerticalGroup, VerticalScroll
+from textual.css.query import NoMatches
 from textual.dom import NoScreen
 from textual.driver import Driver
 from textual.events import AppBlur, AppFocus, MouseScrollDown, MouseScrollUp, MouseUp
@@ -6267,7 +6268,12 @@ class VibeApp(App):  # noqa: PLR0904
         if username is None:
             return
         greeting_message = GreetingMessage(username)
-        chat = self._chat_widget
+        try:
+            chat = self._chat_widget
+        except NoMatches:
+            # Nothing to mount into: this runs in the post-ready worker, which
+            # can still be waiting on the network when the chat goes away.
+            return
         # Mount after banner so it appears below banner and scrolls up with messages
         await chat.mount(greeting_message, after=self._banner)
         self._greeting_message = greeting_message
